sponsor-us	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-12 20:16:09.588+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-10-01 20:03:53.68+00	BECOME A SPONSOR	\N	<div id="fb-root"></div>\n<div class="level4-heading">Help Support Newton Students in STEM Learning and Developing Lifelong Leadership Skills</div>\n<div class="row">\n<div class="col-sm-9 image-border-blue" style="padding-right: 0;"><img style="width: 100%;" src="/images/cheering_photo_2018.jpg"></div>\n<div class="col-sm-3">\n<div class="panel panel-default card" style="background: none; border-width: 2px; margin-bottom: 20px;">&nbsp;\n<div class="row justify-content-center" style="margin-top: 15px; margin-left: 25px;"><form action="https://www.paypal.com/donate" method="post" target="_top"><input name="hosted_button_id" type="hidden" value="YL88EZ9PKRBCE"> <input title="PayPal - The safer, easier way to pay online!" alt="Donate with PayPal button" src="/images/donate_via_paypal.svg" type="image" width="165px"> <img src="https://www.paypal.com/en_US/i/scr/pixel.gif" alt="" width="1" height="1" border="0"></form></div>\n<div class="row justify-content-center" style="margin-top: 15px; margin-left: 25px;"><a href="/donate-by-check/"><img src="/images/donate_via_check.svg" width="165px"></a></div>\n<div class="row justify-content-center" style="margin-top: 37px; margin-left: 100px; transform: scale(2.2);">\n<div class="fb-share-button" data-href="https://ligerbots.org/sponsor" data-layout="button" data-size="large" data-mobile-iframe="false"><a class="fb-xfbml-parse-ignore" href="https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fligerbots.org%2Fsponsor" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Share on Facebook</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class="row justify-content-center" style="margin-top: 57px; margin-left: 100px; transform: scale(2.2);"><a class="twitter-share-button" href="https://twitter.com/share?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw&amp;text=Help%20send%20the%20LigerBots%20to%20the%20Detroit%20FRC%20World%20Championship%21%20%20The%20team%20has%20only%20a%20few%20days%20to%20raise%20%2415k%20for%20fees%2C%20transportation%20and%20lodging.%20Please%20retweet%20%26%20share%20the%20link%20w%2F%20companies%20and%20individuals.%20%23omgrobots%20%23NEFirst%20Learn%20more%20and%20donate" data-size="large" data-show-count="false">Tweet</a></div>\n<div class="row justify-content-center" style="margin-top: 25px; margin-bottom: 15px; margin-left: 25px;"><a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#"><img src="/images/share_by_email.svg" width="165px"></a></div>\n&nbsp; &nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The LigerBots are Newton's all-city FIRST Robotics Competition (FRC) team composed of members from both Newton North and South High Schools. During competition season, students design and build a complex robot to play a new game with a strict 6 week time limit and then compete with that robot in local and regional competitions. Outside of competitions, the team focuses on building technical and 21st century communications, collaboration and leadership skills for team members. In addition, the LigerBots serve as the focal point for project-based learning, participating in STEM outreach in the community to inspire others. Team activities include mentoring younger students in FIRST LEGO League (FLL), appearing at science fairs and community events, and corporate tech events as well as hosting FLL competitions and maker fairs to inspire younger students and the entire community. The LigerBots are proud of the team they have built in the last ten years&mdash;garnering recognition for success in developing a range of skills, from Engineering Inspiration to Imagery to Entrepreneurship to Gracious Professionalism. To support the team, use one of the &ldquo;Donate&rdquo; buttons above, message the team on Facebook, or email <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#cbb8bba4a5b8a4b9e6b9aea7aabfa2a4a5b88ba7a2acaeb9a9a4bfb8e5a4b9ac"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="7102011e1f021e035c03141d1005181e1f02311d18161403131e05025f1e0316">[email&nbsp;protected]</span></a> if you are a corporate sponsor.</p>\n<div class="level4-heading">Why Your Company Should Sponsor the LigerBots</div>\n<p>Now's your chance to support the future engineers and entrepreneurs of Massachusetts. FIRST FRC is a fantastic program promoting STEM education, but building the robot and attending the competitions is quite expensive. Please consider donating to support the LigerBots in their return to the World Championships.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div class="level4-heading">How To Sponsor the LigerBots</div>\n<p>Donations are handled through the Liger Alliance, which is the LigerBots' parent non-profit organization. The Liger Alliance is registered as a 501(c)3, although full approval from the IRS is still in process.</p>\n<p>The best way to make a donation to the team is to send a check to: LigerBots, P.O. Box 66171, Auburndale, MA 02466. Please make the check out to "Liger Alliance," and write "LigerBots" on the check memo line to designate the donation for the LigerBots. If you prefer, you can also donate to us via the PayPal link on this page.</p>\n<!-- *The Liger Alliance is registered as a 501(c)(3) non-profit organization. Contributions to the Newton Schools Foundation are tax-deductible to the extent permitted by law. -->\n<div class="level4-heading" style="margin-bottom: -25px;">The Benefits of Sponsorship</div>\n<p><img src="/images/sponsor_levels_2023.svg" width="100%"></p>\n<div class="level4-heading">Sponsor Resources</div>\n<p>What you get when you sponsor us: <a href="/docs/2024/Sponsor_Benefits_Flyer_2024.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2023-24 Sponsor Benefits Flyer</a><br>Benefits for individual donors: <a href="/docs/2024/Individual_Donor_Benefits_Flyer_2024.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2023-24 Individual Donor Benefits Flyer</a><br>General information about the LigerBots: <a href="/docs/2023/ligerbots_outreach_2023.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2022-23 Outreach Flyer</a><br>Fun facts about the team and our budget: <a href="/docs/2024/ligerbots_infographic_2024.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Infographic</a><br>Information about the team: <a href="/docs/2024/LigerBots_Team_Booklet_2024.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Team Booklet 2024</a><br>Information about our robot: <a href="/docs/2024/LigerBots_Robot_Flyer_2024.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Robot Flyer 2024</a><br>Using our logos: <a href="/docs/2022/LigerBots_Branding_Standards_2022.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Branding Standards</a><br>LigerBots Logo Collection: <a href="/docs/2019/LigerBots_Logos_2019.zip" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Logos</a></p>	\N	\N	<script>\n  // autoload facebook script\n  (function(d, s, id) {\n    var js, fjs = d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];\n    if (d.getElementById(id)) return;\n    js = d.createElement(s); \n    js.id = id;\n    js.src = 'https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/sdk.js#xfbml=1&version=v2.12';\n    fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js, fjs);\n  }(document, 'script', 'facebook-jssdk'));\n</script>\n<script data-cfasync="false" src="/js/email-decode.js"></script>	\N
join	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-10 20:43:04.839+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-09-27 15:10:19.967+00	WELCOME TO THE LIGERBOTS	\N	<center><br><iframe title="YouTube video player" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Y_tL6csFOHc?si=AGVOR4u3GfAQdFFs" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"></iframe></center>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<!-- header -->\n<div class="level4-heading"><a name="open_house"></a> Come to the LigerBots Open House, Mon., 9/30, 6:15 &ndash; 9:00!</div>\n<p>The LigerBots will host an open house for prospective team members on Sept. 30, 2024 from 6:15 &ndash; 9:00 p.m. in the tech ed room at Newton South High School, room 9170. All Newton North and Newton South students are invited. This exciting event will include an introductory presentation about the team and hands-on challenges in many of the skill areas that we learn on our team, like mechanical and electrical engineering, programming, driving robots, CAD (Computer Aided Design), marketing, graphics, photography, and public speaking. Masks are encouraged but not required at LigerBots meetings. Closed-toed shoes are required in the LigerBots shop. For more information, email info@ligerbots.org.</p>\n<div class="level4-heading"><a name="how_to_join_the_team"></a>How to Join the Team</div>\n<p>To join the LigerBots, please go to <a href="https://ligerbots.org/register.php">https://ligerbots.org/register.php</a>. To ensure that the form works properly, please fill it out in the Chrome browser. List a Gmail address that is not one used for Newton Public Schools. Once we have verified your information you will receive an invitation email from the team.</p>\n<!-- /wp:tadv/classic-paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you would simply like to hear more about the team (no commitment required) please fill out the interest form, below, and we will contact you shortly. If you would like to help the LigerBots with mentoring or other opportunities, please <a href="/contact">contact the Coaches and Execs</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In September, meetings will be:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Mondays, 6:30-9:00 p.m., at Newton North in the Engineering Room.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Thursdays, 6:30-9:00 p.m., at Newton South in the Wood Shop, Room 9170.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:tadv/classic-paragraph -->\n<p>Please check the website calendar page (also shown on the home page) for meeting location details.</p>\n<p>Masks are encouraged but not required at LigerBots meetings.</p>\n<!-- /wp:tadv/classic-paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<center><br><iframe id="foo" src="http://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScDs47CsXPi-mNstZ1lCnQ4A6eNmbsb-_S9HotfLp8QFd3acQ/viewform?embedded=true" width="640" height="980" frameborder="0" marginwidth="0" marginheight="0" sandbox="">Loading…</iframe></center>	\N	\N	\N	\N
gallery	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-12 20:48:24.021+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-09-27 15:10:19.967+00	PHOTOS	\N	<center style="margin-bottom: 2.25em; word-wrap: break-word;">\n<h5 class="gallery-link">To see all LigerBots photos: <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/ligerbots/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">flickr.com/photos/ligerbots/</a></h5>\n<h5 class="gallery-link">To see all LigerBots videos: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/c/ligerbots" target="_blank" rel="noopener">youtube.com/c/ligerbots</a></h5>\n</center><center>\n<h1><span style="color: #e03e2d;">TO BE DEVELOPED</span></h1>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<iframe class="giphy-embed" src="https://giphy.com/embed/NMMj3u6gbrDdCTvUy0" width="480" height="418" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe>\n<p><a href="https://giphy.com/gifs/soyproductiva-sp-work-in-progress-soy-productiva-NMMj3u6gbrDdCTvUy0">via GIPHY</a></p>\n</center>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>	\N	\N	\N	\N
fll	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-12 20:43:32.74+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-09-27 15:10:19.967+00	FLL	\N	<div class="level4-heading">\n<figure><img style="max-width: 100%;" src="https://farm5.staticflickr.com/4541/37808387264_34b49ca6ca_k.jpg"></figure>\n<div class="image-border-blue">&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n<!-- /wp:tadv/classic-paragraph --><!-- wp:tadv/classic-paragraph -->\n<div class="level4-heading">FIRST<small>&reg;</small> LEGO<small>&reg;</small> League (FLL) Newton Qualifier and<br>Massachusetts East Championship</div>\n<!-- /wp:tadv/classic-paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The LigerBots host the FLL Newton Qualifier every year at Newton North High School on the last Saturday before Thanksgiving, and often host the Massachusetts East FLL Championship at the high school in mid-December.<a href="https://flic.kr/s/aHBqjB3Rj6">The last Newton Qualifier</a> was November 18, 2023, and the <a href="https://flic.kr/s/aHBqjB7CE7">Massachusetts East FLL Championship</a> was December 16, 2023.</p>\n<p>At the these FLL events, teams of students in grades 4 to 8 compete using LEGO robots they design, build, and program to perform complex tasks in a novel challenge created by FIRST every year. The 2023 challenge was called <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zI_vz9YUw1g">Masterpiece</a>, which had an arts theme. (A unified theme carries through each year in all of FIRST's programs, from K-12.) FLL teams also compete by giving presentations they have researched and created on a topic related to the game theme. You can learn more about the 2023 season on the <a href="https://www.first-lego-league.org/en/2023-24-season/the-masterpiece-season">FIRST website.</a> The FIRST 2024/25 game is called <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4JV7x014U0I">Submerged</a>, with an ocean theme. FIRST will launch the 2024/25 season on August 6, 2024.</p>\n<p>The LigerBots host a STEAM expo at the MA East FLL Championship, with hands-on activities for kids in the fields of science, technology, engineering, art, and math, presented by team members and by local organizations. The public is always invited to watch our tournaments and to enjoy the activities at the STEAM expo. More than 1000 people usually attend our two FLL events, including FLL team members, families, LigerBots volunteers, and members of the public.&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Our STEAM expo at the 2023 MA East FLL Championship included 11 activities provided by local companies and organizations, plus 15 more activities and six robot demonstrations offered by the LigerBots and other FIRST Robotics Competition (FRC) and FIRST Tech Challenge (FTC) teams. If your organization would like to bring a hands-on activity for kids to our next STEAM expo, please email <strong><a href="mailto:fll@ligerbots.org">fll@ligerbots.org</a></strong>.</p>\n<p>You can find hundreds of photos from the 2023 events on the <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/ligerbots/albums/">LigerBots Flickr</a> page.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:tadv/classic-paragraph -->\n<div class="level4-heading">FLL Information Night</div>\n<!-- /wp:tadv/classic-paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The LigerBots will host its annual FIRST LEGO League (FLL) information night on Saturday, June 22, 2024, from 3:00 to 4:30 p.m., at the<a href="https://www.wpsinstitute.org/wps-cll"> WPS Community Learning Lab,</a> 160 Herrick Road, Newton, MA 02459. If you would like to attend &mdash; or cannot attend but are interested &mdash; please fill out <a href="https://forms.gle/sZV4F4t8m43R1Fti8">this form.</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If you cannot attend, a link to the presentation will be posted on this page after the event.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:tadv/classic-paragraph -->\n<p>For more background on the FLL program, here is the <a href="https://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/fll">official FLL website</a> and <a href="https://www.firstinspires.org/about/vision-and-mission">FIRST&rsquo;s mission statement</a>, this year&rsquo;s <a href="https://info.firstinspires.org/first-dive">FLL challenge and season info,</a> and the <a href="https://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/fll/calendar">FLL season calendar</a>. You can also email <strong><a href="mailto:fll@ligerbots.org">fll@ligerbots.org</a></strong> for more information.</p>\n<!-- /wp:tadv/classic-paragraph --><!-- wp:tadv/classic-paragraph -->\n<div class="level4-heading">About FIRST<small>&reg;</small> LEGO<small>&reg;</small> League</div>\n<!-- /wp:tadv/classic-paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>FLL immerses students in grades pre-K to 8 in real-world scientific and technological problems, such as food safety or recycling. There are three levels of FLL based on the students&rsquo; grade: FLL Discover, FLL Explore, and FLL Challenge. FLL Discover is a playful introduction to STEM for children in grades pre-K to 1. FLL Explore, for students in grades 2 to 4, helps students explore while they learn about the design and coding of FLL robots by using powered LEGO&reg; bricks to create solutions to problems. FLL Challenge is a competition for students in grades 4 to 8 that teaches them to build and program autonomous LEGO&reg; robots that can compete on a 4&rsquo; x 8&rsquo; field in the annual robot game designed by the FIRST organization, performing assigned missions such as moving a ball or flipping a switch. FLL Challenge teams also research a real-world problem within guidelines provided by FIRST and design solutions that can be presented to judges at an FLL tournament.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In addition to helping to teach students about STEAM through hands-on activities, experience in FLL is good preparation for the high-school-level FIRST Robotics Competition (FRC) program, whether with the LigerBots or any other FRC team. The LigerBots are committed to doing what the team can to support FLL programs, including acting as an information clearinghouse and supporting FLL coaches who are figuring out how to get an FLL team up and running.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>New teams are typically formed by two to three parents interested in providing an FLL experience for their kids. Teams typically meet once or twice a week for two to three hours, and the season is approximately 10 weeks long. Parent coaches do not have to be engineers or scientists! The challenge is designed to be solved by kids. Teams can have up to 10 student members. While teams tend to come and go as children enter and then age out of the FLL program, there are a few legacy teams that occasionally have openings for new team members.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:tadv/classic-paragraph -->\n<p>The first requirement for forming a team is to have space for a 4' x 8' game table. It costs about $1100 in materials to start an FLL team and about $500 in recurring costs each year. Startup costs include a robot controller module kit (<a href="https://www.lego.com/en-us/categories/robots-for-kids">Spike</a> or EV3), which is about $400, a set of specialized LEGOs called Technics, that costs about another $500, and materials to build a table, which cost about $150. Recurring expenses include a $250 team registration fee that goes to FIRST, a &ldquo;challenge set&rdquo; sold by FIRST for about $100 that includes a game mat and LEGOs specific to that year&rsquo;s challenge, and a registration fee of about $100 per competition for each level the team makes it to. The cost can be divided by the number of participants, or the team can apply for grants. Of course, if teams want to spend more money, they can, but they do not need to. Here is the <a href="https://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/fll/challenge/pricing-and-payment">FLL pricing and payment payment page</a> on the FIRST website.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;For more information on how to start a team, you can visit the <a href="https://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/fll/start-a-team">FIRST&reg; website</a>, or you can email the LigerBots at fll@ligerbots.org.</p>	\N	\N	\N	\N
contact	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-11 20:42:37.299+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-09-27 15:10:19.967+00	CONTACT THE LIGERBOTS	\N	<center>\n<h4><a href="mailto:execs@ligerbots.org">Email the executive board</a></h4>\n<h4><a href="mailto:coaches@ligerbots.org">Email the coaches</a></h4>\n<br>If you are trying to learn about FLL, or looking for help forming a team, please send email to <a href="mailto:fll@ligerbots.org">fll@ligerbots.org</a>. <br><br>If you are an NPS high school student or parent/guardian and want to register with the LigerBots, please go to our <a href="/register">registration page.</a></center>	\N	\N	\N	\N
current-sponsors	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-12 20:28:55.33+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-09-27 15:10:19.967+00	CURRENT SPONSORS	\N	<div class="row spr-first-section">\n<div class="big-sprs"><iframe src="/images/sponsor_page_full_2024a.svg" sandbox=""></iframe></div>\n<div class="small-sprs text-margins"><iframe src="/images/sponsor_page_narrow_2024a.svg" sandbox=""></iframe></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n</div>	\N	\N	\N	\N
calendar	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-12 20:36:55.842+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-09-27 15:10:19.967+00	Calendar	\N	<div class="row side-margins bottom-margin">\n<div class="col-xs-12"><iframe class="calendar" src="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/embed?src=c_r2405nbigo9eqb06kbvnk51bcc%40group.calendar.google.com&amp;ctz=America%2FNew_York" sandbox=""></iframe></div>\n</div>	\N	\N	\N	\N
outreach	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-12 20:41:54.06+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-09-27 15:10:19.967+00	OUTREACH	\N	<div class="level4-heading">\n<div class="image-border-blue"><img style="max-width: 75%;" src="https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49607319987_ca4b19f54d_3k.jpg"></div>\n</div>\n<div class="level4-heading">Our Outreach Work</div>\n<p>The LigerBots pride themselves on our strong relationships in our community, and the work we do to motivate others to get involved in STEM. Click on the links below to explore some of our interactions with the community!</p>\n<div class="level4-heading">AMP</div>\n<p>Click <a href="/amp">here</a> to learn more about the Awesome Mentorship Program.</p>\n<div class="level4-heading">FLL</div>\n<p>Click <a href="/fll">here</a> to learn more about our work with FLL.</p>\n<div class="level4-heading">Educational Resources</div>\n<p>Click <a href="/educational-resources">here</a> to access our STEAM Activity Flyers and our Whitepapers.</p>	\N	\N	\N	\N
about	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-10 19:57:17.73+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-09-27 15:10:19.967+00	ABOUT THE LIGERBOTS	\N	<div class="level4-heading"><a name="about_first"></a>About FIRST</div>\n<p>FIRST ("For Inspiration and Recognition of Science and Technology") was founded in 1989 by Dean Kamen, inventor of the Segway human transport.</p>\n<p>FIRST was founded to help create the next generation of scientists, inventors, and engineers by providing high school students with challenges that foster an interest and develop skills in engineering, mathematics, and science. In addition, by having students work in teams, FIRST helps build self-confidence as well as teamwork and leadership skills.</p>\n<p>Each year, FIRST develops a robotics challenge that teams of students, mentored by faculty and community participants, work to solve. Teams design and build a robot to tackle specific elements of each year's challenge and then compete against robots and teams, first in regional competitions and then in the world championship in St. Louis.</p>\n<p>To simulate real world engineering challenges, student teams are given six to eight weeks in which to build a robot that can succeed in a competitive environment.</p>\n<p>During the build season, students work through all the steps of the design and building process by brainstorming, planning, and designing, prototyping, testing, fabricating, assembling and constantly improving their designs.</p>\n<p>Teams also work on the business side of the venture by creating and maintaining budgets, organizing fundraising, and developing promotional materials.</p>\n<p>Finally, in addition to all the work directly linked to creating the robot and funding the team, FIRST promotes both community involvement and "gracious professionalism." While everyone loves to win, FIRST is not about winning in the traditional sense. Winning in FIRST is linked to continuing the vision of its founder: to provide inspiration and recognition of the value of science and technology. Teams are expected to mentor new teams and to participate in community events which promote science and technology. They are also expected to be good sports and to help team members and other teams, especially at competitions when teams help their competitors compete by sharing tools, parts, and experience.</p>\n<div class="level4-heading"><a name="about_us"></a>About the LigerBots</div>\n<p>The LigerBots is a <a href="https://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/frc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FIRST FRC</a> robotics team composed of members from both Newton North and Newton South High Schools in Massachusetts.</p>\n<p>Students participating in LigerBots design and build a complex robot that plays a game, which is different each year. They have about eight weeks to design, build, and program their machine so that team members can control it on the playing field.</p>\n<p>At competitions, teams are grouped in alliances of three teams, each alliance working cooperatively to outscore another alliance.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;In past years, we have designed robots to play Frisbee and basketball, stack packing crates, and put totes on large balance beams. You can see the 2020 robot challenge at <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gmiYWTmFRVE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gmiYWTmFRVE</a>.</p>\n<p>In addition, the team is run like a small business. The team not only builds a robot, but students have to build a brand, create a business plan, organize and volunteer at community events, build teamwork skills, find sponsors and mentors, raise funds, and of course, still complete their homework!</p>\n<p>The LigerBots is a student-run team, guided by volunteer adult mentors expert in various fields, and by team veterans. In addition to the design and construction of the robot, LigerBots students are expected to take responsibility for all other aspects of the team, including fundraising, marketing, and publicity.</p>\n<p>Students on the LigerBots are also actively involved in community outreach and service. Ultimately, the goal of FIRST, and therefore, the goal of the LigerBots, is to take those principles in excellence of STEM education and spread them into the community at every level.</p>\n<div class="level4-heading">Student Activities</div>\n<p>Designing, building and operating the robot are all challenging opportunities, but there is much more to our team than the robot. We need students who are willing to work on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Business &amp; marketing</li>\n<li>Fundraising</li>\n<li>Publicity</li>\n<li>Graphic Design</li>\n<li>Accounting</li>\n<li>Web design and management</li>\n<li>Mechanical &amp; electrical design</li>\n<li>Construction</li>\n<li>Programming</li>\n<li>CAD drawing</li>\n</ul>\n<div class="level4-heading"><a name="team_partners"></a>Other Team Partners</div>\n<p>A selection of some of the other FIRST teams we have made friends with, helped, or been helped by over the years: <a href="http://www.stormgears.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stormgears FRC (5422)</a> In 2018, the Stormgears graciously allowed us, and other teams, to use their practice field on many occasions. This was tremendously helpful in developing our autonomous routines, plus allowed for more realistic driver practice. Again in 2020, the Stormgears held a pre-season scrimmage for 6 teams which helped us practice before our first real competition. They also generously allowed us to spend an entire weekend using their field to work on our control code and autonomous routines. <a href="http://www.nutrons.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NUTRONS (125)</a> Team 125, The Nutrons, is a team organized by Northeastern University, and includes members from four local high schools. Prior to our rookie year, they loaned us an old robot that we refit in time for the Beantown Blitz. <a href="http://www.cybergnomes2013.ca/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cybergnomes (2013)</a> The Cybergnomes are a FRC team from Stayner, Ontario. In 2010, they gave us an award for "Best Mascot". The LigerBots then hosted the team during the 2011, 2012, and 2013 competitions in Boston. In 2018, our pits were across from each other on the Daly Field at the Detroit World Championships. We enjoyed renewing our friendship and competing with and against them. <a href="http://rosie.agawamrobotics.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Rosie Robotics (839)</a> Rosie Robotics has helped the LigerBots (and countless other teams) many times. When we found that the motor that we used for our arm wasn't allowed in Logo Motion, they gave us a legal motor, mounting hardware, and advice. LigerCubs (FLL 2437) The FLL team "The LigerCubs" were coached by former LigerBots coach Deb Lund. After helping the LigerBots create many Newton FLL teams, she left the LigerBots to start her own FLL team. The LigerBots are proud to have inspired Coach Lund and her children. LigerPandas (FTC 4377) The LigerPandas were an FTC team created and sponsored by the LigerBots in 2011, 2012 and 2013. They were made up of Chinese foreign exchange students and a number of LigerBot volunteers; this made them the first FIRST team ever to be created for foreign exchange students.</p>	\N	\N	\N	\N
educational-resources	published	457dbbb9-5eb6-491d-9c18-095db7fffc84	2024-09-12 20:45:31.775+00	cfd32bb9-5bce-4724-8ef3-1a01b9714c9f	2024-09-27 15:10:19.967+00	EDUCATIONAL RESOURCES	\N	<div class="level4-heading">STEAM Activity Flyers</div>\n<ul style="list-style-type: square;">\n<li>STEAM activity and information&nbsp; flyer: <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1H2kvECT1g4XtjEV8tXPgPf4LmNGfOjIB/view?usp=drive_link">Articulating Model Hand</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/balloon_car_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Balloon Car</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/binary_beads_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Binary Beads</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/brushbots_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BrushBots</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/paper_airplane_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dart Paper Airplanes</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/elephant_toothpaste.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Elephant Toothpaste</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/scratch_game_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jumping Game in Scratch</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/lightsaber_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mini-lightsabers</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/moving_flexagon_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Moving Flexagon Origami</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/needle_compass.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Needle Compass</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/origami_double_pyramid_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Origami Double Pyramid</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/skeleton_xray_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Skeleton Handprint "X-Ray"</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/slime_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Slime</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/solar_oven_activity.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Solar Ovens</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/spool_racer.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Spool Racer</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/sunbutter_jelly_robot_commands_easier.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sunbutter and Jelly Robot Commands, Easier Set</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/sunbutter_jelly_robot_commands_harder.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sunbutter and Jelly Robot Commands, Harder Set</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qjPtGAoyVWEo4RXk7ZAbytEI0DCFy-7V/view?usp=drive_link">Skeleton Handprint "X-Ray"</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/tangrams.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tangrams</a></li>\n<li>STEAM activity and information flyer: <a href="/docs/activities/3d_printers.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">3D Printer</a></li>\n<li><a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CBfb-2h1e67nsEJVC6sforK8qsbE9PU4/view?usp=drive_link">STEAM activity booklet with all activities</a></li>\n</ul>\n<div class="level4-heading">LigerBots White Papers</div>\n<ul style="list-style-type: square;">\n<li>Distance Learning: <a href="/docs/whitepapers/Distance_Learning_Whitepaper.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Distance Learning Whitepaper</a></li>\n<li>Vision Processing: <a href="/docs/whitepapers/LigerBots_Vision_Whitepaper.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Vision Whitepaper</a></li>\n<li>Camera Latency: <a href="/docs/whitepapers/LigerBots_Camera_Latency_Whitepaper.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Camera Latency Whitepaper</a></li>\n<li>Electrical Test Bench: <a href="/docs/whitepapers/LigerBots_Test_Bench_Whitepaper.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Electric Testbench Whitepaper</a></li>\n<li>Cleanup Bot 9000: <a href="/docs/whitepapers/cleanup_bot_9000.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LigerBots Cleanup Bot 9000 Whitepaper</a></li>\n</ul>	\N	\N	\N	\N
